# Transport & queue

## Wire contract

Events:

- `POST {url}/v1/events`
- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <tal_sk_ key>`
- Body (plain JSON, no `input` wrapper):

```json
{ "events": [ { "message": "..." } ] }
```

Spans (when tracing is enabled):

- `POST {url}/v1/spans`
- Same Bearer header
- Body: `{ "spans": [ { ... } ] }`
- `SpanTransport` constructs its **own** Guzzle client. Do not install `GuzzleMiddleware` on ingest transports.

Analytics (server-side; no autocapture, no cookie jar):

- `POST {url}/v1/analytics`
- Body: `{ "events": [ { ... } ] }`
- `AnalyticsTransport` constructs its **own** Guzzle client.
- `track` requires `userId` and/or `anonymousId` (browser ids forwarded by the caller)
- Core `enableAnalytics` defaults true; when false the facade no-ops. Silverstripe YAML / `TALARIA_ENABLE_ANALYTICS` defaults off.

- Even a single leftover event, span, or analytics item is a batch of one
- `extra` → `extraJson` (JSON **string**); `tags` are string→string
- Flat `userId` / `url` — not nested `user` / `request`
- First-class `exception` (`ExceptionDataDto` / frames with `functionName`) — never put `exception_class` / `file` / `line` / `code` in `extra`
- `platform: "php"` on all PHP captures (exceptions and messages); keep raw `stackTrace` string alongside structured frames

## EventQueue drain triggers

| Trigger | Config | When |
| ------- | ------ | ---- |
| Size | `maxBatchSize` (default 50) | Buffer reaches N |
| Age | `flushIntervalMs` (default 2000) | Checked on each enqueue |
| Explicit | `flush()` / `close()` | Always drain |
| Shutdown | `register_shutdown_function` | Drain remainder |

PHP FPM has no background timer — age is checked on enqueue, not via a wall-clock thread.

## Reliability

- Short HTTP timeout (2–3s)
- No unbounded retries; on 429 log warning and drop/backoff once
- Transport failures must not crash the host app. Queues catch every `\Throwable` from a transport; `checkIn`, `reportClient`, `flush` and flag loads swallow and log. Transport log lines go through `FailSafe::logRateLimited` (one per signal per minute)
- Call `fastcgi_finish_request()` when available before shutdown network I/O
- On ingest `retry: false` (or known permanent class names when `retry` is absent): drop the batch, log once, and disable events **and** spans **and** analytics for the rest of this PHP process. Message contains `lacks required scope` disables **that signal only**. Quota / rate-limit (`retry: true`) and 5xx must **not** disable. FPM workers reuse the singleton — a new worker after deploy picks up a rotated key.
